  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Stormbringer: Binder of Storms summons Thunder Orbs from Deluge's Conduction (#12920)",
  "contract": [
    "#12920: Binder of Storms 707542 reads 'Damage dealt by Conduction now has a 60% chance to summon a Thunder",
    "Orb.' #3133 gave it a spell_proc row that selects Conduction 567560, and",
    "stormbringer-fix-thunder-orb-summons-binder proves it with Conduction cast directly. In play Conduction is",
    "always a triggered cast: Deluge and Torrential Wrath cast it from a hit-result hook",
    "(stormbringer-deluge-triggers-conduction-12687). A proc entry without PROC_ATTR_TRIGGERED_CAN_PROC skips",
    "triggered spells in Aura::GetProcEffectMask, and Conduction does not carry SPELL_ATTR3_NOT_A_PROC, so no orb",
    "ever appeared. The row now sets AttributesMask 2. A level 60 Stormbringer with Binder of Storms casts Deluge",
    "807713 12 times at an enemy; each cast triggers one Conduction (asserted), and at a 60% ProcChance the",
    "chance of no proc in 12 hits is 0.4^12 = 1.7e-5. Deluge costs 50 Static (803102), so Static is set before",
    "each cast, and spell hit rating forces every cast to land."
  ],
